**Digital Pedagogy Coach — ****10 Professional Accountabilities**

Graeme Wright  ·  Quality Team  ·  Weston College Group  ·  18-Month Pilot 2026–27

| **#** | **Responsibility** | **Actions** | **Phase** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1** | **Map digital and subject-specific skills to the framework** | **·  **Complete HoA conversations (target 20 by end of May) **·  **Compile one-page mapping summary of what areas are doing, gaps, and good practice **·  **Share summary with Neil Davies by end of May **·  **Present mapping picture at a CQRP or TLAM group in June **·  **Use mapping to inform QIP actions and digital hours in Business Plans for 2026/27 | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |
| **2** | **Teams environment audit with HoA and Digital Leads; follow-up training** | **·  **Design Teams Digital Health Check as a Microsoft Form (10 items, traffic-light rated) **·  **Run pilot audits with 3–4 areas before end of May **·  **Book follow-up coaching within 2 weeks of any audit identifying gaps **·  **Share Health Check results with TLAMs **·  **Embed termly Health Check as Digital Leads responsibility from September 2026 | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |
| **3** | **Clarify Digital Leads vs Digital Champions; engage both structures** | **·  **Write one-page Digital Lead role description and share with TLAMs by end of April **·  **Identify named Digital Leads per area through TLAM conversations **·  **Formally induct Digital Leads at the start of 2026/27 **·  **Plan Digital Champions 2026/27 programme — recruitment, structure, and projects **·  **Recruit Digital Champions cohort in first two weeks of September 2026 | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |
| **4** | **Design, set up and deliver accessibility by design workshops — iTrent, termly, NSI** | **·  **Design 60-minute Accessibility by Design workshop **·  **Book first session on iTrent for May or June (target 20+ attendees) **·  **Confirm NSI slot with coordinator for August 2026 cohort (20-minute version) **·  **Book termly iTrent sessions for 2026/27 (October, January, April) **·  **Gather feedback after each session and iterate content | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |
| **5** | **Create accessibility support videos for Digital Foundations on SharePoint** | **·  **Record 5 screen-recorded videos (under 5 minutes each): Accessibility Checker, alt text, heading styles, captions, accessible links **·  **Publish videos to SharePoint 'Accessibility by Design — Quick Guides' section by end of July **·  **Share SharePoint link with all TLAMs in September **·  **Add one new video per term from September as gaps emerge from coaching | **Phase 2** Build Infrastructure |
| **6** | **IT roadmap and next steps — Learning Without Barriers for ESOL and SEND** | **·  **Audit AT licence status — Read & Write Gold, Tobii, Proloquo2Go, Clicker **·  **Hold joint meeting with IT and SEND team (Liz Burkley, Lois Knight) in July **·  **Agree specific next steps with named owners from the meeting **·  **Write one-page roadmap and share with Neil Davies by end of August **·  **Review progress at the start of each term from September 2026 | **Phase 2** Build Infrastructure |
| **7** | **Videos and resources for Assistive Technology support** | **·  **Record 3 core AT videos: Immersive Reader (show to all learners at induction); Live Captions in Teams; Read & Write Gold staff guide **·  **Publish to 'Assistive Technology for Staff' SharePoint section by end of July **·  **Distribute to ESOL, Learning Support, FIP, and HAC TLAMs in September **·  **Add specialist AT videos (Tobii, Proloquo2Go) from September once licences confirmed | **Phase 2** Build Infrastructure |
| **8** | **Coaching for AI support and training** | **·  **Compile AI training log — areas, staff numbers, content covered, one testimonial per area **·  **Draft college AI position statement for staff (three sentences) and share with Neil Davies for sign-off **·  **Design a 45-minute 'AI in Teaching — Starting Safely' session and publish on iTrent **·  **Deliver session to 3–4 priority areas before end of June **·  **Embed AI content as a standing COG theme from 2026/27 | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |
| **9** | **Lead digital skills training — Jisc, ETF, curated sources; Century for learners** | **·  **Confirm Jisc Discovery Tool institutional setup with Jisc **·  **Run pilot with 5–8 staff before September to test the process **·  **Write one-page TLAM guide: 'Digital Skills Assessment — What to Do in September' **·  **Map Century Tech EDS diagnostics into 2026/27 learner induction plan **·  **Confirm Century plan with HoAs before end of June | **Phase 2** Build Infrastructure |
| **10** | **Represent Weston College in external networks; horizon scanning** | **·  **Populate 2026/27 external events calendar — BETT (January), Digifest (March), ETF/SET conference, Jisc BDC Community of Practice (biannual) **·  **Block time for external events before the year fills up **·  **Attend one external event per half-term from September 2026 **·  **Share a one-paragraph write-up with quality colleagues after each event **·  **Bring one external-sourced item to each termly Teach Meet from September | **Phase 1** Finish & Formalise |

*Phase 1: April–June 2026  ·  Phase 2: July–August 2026 (infrastructure build)  ·  Phase 3: 2026/27 academic year (scale and sustain)  ·  Governance reviews: July 2026, January 2027, October 2027, December 2027*